    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only executable test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement: on a successful owner create, a line containing the owner id and the `memberId` is now emitted via the logger named `NOTIFY`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New function class** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueOwnerWelcome.java` \u2014 a single-public-method OfficeFloor step that reads the built/saved `Owner` via `@Val` and logs `welcome owner id={} memberId={}` through `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")`, mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step.\n\n2. **Wired it into the create pipeline** in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step after `audit` (so the id and memberId are already assigned) and before the warning-derivation steps, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors so the create still commits as one boundary. It only runs on the successful `create` branch, not the idempotent `existing` short-circuit.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes (the captured NOTIFY line contains both the owner id and its memberId), and the full `./mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
